                            | what is DDOS ??|            
                            |----------------|
            DDOS is method that uses to crash your server by sending a mellions of SYN to the 
            server from one attacker using a fake ip address and the server send SYN+ACK 
            (waiting for final ACK from client but never response by it) that makes the queue full 
            and the other client can not connect to your server anymore

    so that why the kernel has SYN queue it allocate a lightwight struct in SYN queue until it receive 
    final ACk it copie it from SYN queue to accept queue and remove it from SYN queue 
    (wait accept to build an entry in fd table for your proccess and return that fd to user space)


        this happen in listen function not accept
        {
            SYN QUEUE
                Client SYN --> SYN Queue --> (SYN+ACK) --> wait for final ACK
            After handshake finishes --> put in accept queue --> wait for accept()
        }   
        Connections here are ready, but the app does not see them until accept()

            // cat /proc/sys/net/core/somaxconn
            default backlog in linux for listen is 4096
            even you config listen with 10000 the kernel will replace it with 4096 (only if you type number of backlog > 4096)

