         Key Points from Diagram

NIC only knows about DMA buffers — it has no socket knowledge.

CPU interrupt triggers the kernel to process the packet.

SoftIRQ (net_rx_action) handles protocol layers and puts data into the socket queue.

epoll waits on the socket’s wait queue, which is woken by the kernel when data arrives.

User process wakes and reads the packet — data is never executed, protected by NX.
