Key Points  :

        HardIRQ (NIC interrupt handler)

        Runs immediately, in kernel mode

        Minimal work to avoid blocking other interrupts

        SoftIRQ (NET_RX)

        Runs later, still in kernel context

        Handles the network stack and socket queue

        epoll_wait()

        Sleeps in user space

        Woken only when the kernel adds data to the socket receive queue

        DMA

        Already copied the packet before any interrupt handler runs

